// T-54-3 obr. 1951 — reference outlines for the K0 overlay gate.
//
// Closed loops in metres in the vehicle frame (+Y up, +Z bow, +X port), one set per view. Side and
// front are TRACED from a drawing (see each view's note); the plan is still drawn from tables. The
// bake's silhouette is compared with their union by intersection-over-union. Every number below
// is traced to `docs/vehicles/t-54.md` (Reference anatomy) except where a comment says
// BLUEPRINT: those extents (the turret's plan and dome, the sprocket and idler centres) have no
// documented value yet and are copied from the model's own blueprint, which is why every view
// is `Target` — the outline is not the drawing until the owner traces R1
// (`docs/vehicles/refs/t-54.md`) over the overlay PNG (`cargo run -p tools -- outline-overlay`).
// Flip a view to `Locked` in the PR that does that, never before. Until then each view holds a
// FLOOR: the IoU measured the day it was authored, so the silhouette cannot drift away from the
// drawing while the bar waits (the owner delegated the call, 2026-09-05).
